title: Design as an Attitude
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

<<<
Designing is not a profession but an attitude.
<<< [[László Moholy-Nagy]], //Vision in Motion//, 1947

Design as a way of approaching any problem, with any material, at any scale. Not a job title and not a style.

[[Alice Rawsthorn]] used the phrase as the title of her 2018 book.

People I put in this line: [[László Moholy-Nagy]], [[The Eameses]], [[Enzo Mari]], [[Victor Papanek]].

If design is an attitude, then [[The object is the visible result of a way of working]].

See [[Doing Design is Important; Being a Designer is not.]], [[If you can Design one thing, you can design anything]], [[Designer]], [[BauHaus]], [[Way-it-should-be-ness]]
